# {{.Name}}

A [Dygo](https://{{.Framework}}) application with the modular layout.

```
main.go              main.ts: load config, create the app, listen
app.module.go        app.module.ts: the root module (AppModule) and app options
app_test.go          e2e tests for the whole app
src/
  config/            typed configuration from the environment and .env
  database/          the database connection, a global module
  health/            /health/live and /health/ready (pings the database)
  common/            types shared by features, such as Pagination
  modules/           feature modules: dygo g resource <name> adds one here
```

```sh
cp .env.example .env     # after a fresh clone: .env is git ignored, dygo new made yours
dygo start               # http://localhost:9900, API docs at /docs
dygo start -watch        # restart on every change
go test ./...
dygo check               # validate the module wiring without starting
go build -o app .        # build the binary
docker build -t app .    # build the image
dygo routes              # the route table
dygo g entity User       # src/modules/users/users.go, asks for the fields
dygo g crud User         # module, service, controller and test, imported in app.module.go
```
